### Custom
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
bin

# Compiled binary from `go build ./cmd/api` (the Web/API server). README builds
# it as `./aurora-api` (matches the /aurora-* rule above), but a bare `go build`
# emits `./api`; a stale copy was once committed (TASK-266, ISS-262) so keep the
# root-level name ignored too.
/api

# Core dumps (from crashes / panics in tests or binaries)
core
core.*

### JetBrains template
# CMake
cmake-build-*/

# File-based project format
*.iws

# IntelliJ
out/

### Go template
# Binaries for programs and plugins.
# Anchored to the repo root: `just build` emits `./aurora` and the release
# cross-builds emit `./aurora-<os>-<arch>`. A non-anchored `**/aurora`
# would ALSO match the `cmd/aurora/` source directory and silently ignore
# every test file under it — which is exactly what happened here.
/aurora
/aurora-*
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/
data/
test/data/
.worktrees/
